  "title": "Rasuwagadhi and Syabrubesi (SkySat) — Post-event Imagery",
  "description": "High-resolution SkySat coverage of two focal points on the flood corridor, acquired 02:00 UTC on 27 August 2026, about a day after the flood. One collect covers the Rasuwagadhi border crossing, the other Syabrubesi and the upper Trishuli. At roughly 0.8 m ground sample distance these resolve individual buildings, bridges and road sections — far finer detail than the 3.8 m PlanetScope scenes. Both carry 50% cloud with a clear fraction near 8%, so usable ground is patchy but sharp where visible. 2 scenes; each Item carries the available visual, pansharpened, udm assets.",
